#82002
"Edge of the Drifts"
"Great drifts block any passage to the east or west, a spectacular reminder of

the forces of nature.  The drifts end abruptly to the north as a chasm yawns

into the snowy black some mindless distance beneath the trail.  This region

seems to have seen quite a bit of activity recently, as a trail of sorts has

been trampled into the snow by the passing of a few giant humanoid creatures. 

The trail ends abruptly at the cliff edge, and continues south on a slope into

a depression.


An ancient stone marker stands a few meters from the cliff edge.

"
""
