"ancient stone marker sign"
"In ancient times this might have been a sign indicating landmarks that lay

ahead on the trail.  Intricate, spidery runes have been carved into the face

of the marker, most of which have been obliterated through ages of weather. 

Arrows seem to point northward, off the cliff edge, and eastward, into a great

snowdrift, although what is supposed to be in those directions is impossible

to discern from the writing.

"
