#82004
"Mountainside Path - Turn in the Trail"
"The packed icy trail turns abruptly to the north here, where the rocky

overhang above is littered with icicles, some as large as a man.  The grey

rock of the cliffside to the east and south is covered with a fine dusting of

snow, but the trail is free of drifts and shows evidence of the recent

activity of a number of large, humanoid creatures.  Narrower than the trail to

the north and south, the pass here is still wide enough to easily accomodate a

wagon and its team of horses.  Past a snowbank on the northwest edges of the

trail, through the swirling snow, the panorama of the Dragonspires stretches

as far as you can see.

"
""
