#82005
"The Fangs of the Dragonspires"
"Grand icicles, as thick as an ancient oak at their base, flow from the

overhang above to the chasm edge on the western side of the trail.  The trail

narrows abruptly here -- a flat space thirty paces across is all that stands

between the eastern cliff wall and the chasm to the west.  Snow-capped

mountains stretch for an eternity; framed between mighty icicles that flow

from the overhanging cliff above, the view is breathtaking.  A few patches of

blood lie splashed on the rocks at your feet, evidence of some greater

predator than the yetis which are said to roam this region.

"
""
