#82006
"Mountainside Trail - Littered with Boulders"
"The snow in this area has been churned and packed down by something very large

and terribly heavy.  Dark red patches stain the snow in a few places along the

trail, more evidence that this area is frequented by a large predator. 

Boulders ranging in size from a few feet to the size of a small cottage litter

the trail, sentinels of rock and ice that certainly bore witness to the

carnage that occurred not long ago.  The trail is very wide and the rocky

overhang visible along the trail to the south is not evident here.  Through

the swirling snow west of the trail, the panorama of the Dragonspires

stretches for miles.

"
