#82007
"Treacherous Footing"
"Towering taller to the north, the mountain above seems impossibly large and

the trail a narrow ribbon winding its way desperately forward.  The trail

narrows dramatically as one heads north, forcing travellers to hug the

frost-rimed rock of the mountain face to the east.  Large, heavy footprints

pack down the fresh snow on the trail, evidence that something has travelled

here recently.  The trail continues at an upslope to the north, although the

footprints are evident no further in that direction.

"
"[Dalthas] follow trig from south of here is messed up, must be $n instead of $N

