#82009
"Narrow Trail - Collapsing Mountainside"
"At one time, perhaps centuries ago, the trail must have been wide enough here

to provide a respite from the treacherous sections below and above.  The land

is flat and the cliff's edge on the eastern side of the trail far from the

chasm that parallels the trail on the west.  Unfortunately, at some point the

cliff edge collapsed onto the wide eastern part of the trail, flooding it with

a treacherous pile of rock and ice.  What remains of the trail shows no signs

of any but animal activity.

"
"[Maurtock] pile extra here

"
