#82010
"Treacherous Footing"
"Blasted by a wind from the chasm below, the mountainside has lost all traces

of snow and instead collected a thin, icy coating along the grey rock face. 

Stretching above and below you, the mountain is incomprehensibly large and

seems immune to the forces ravaging it.  The trail here, while wide enough to

accomodate the travel of a man leading a horse, has sections that have fallen

away, leaving dangerous gaps that must be jumped.  The wind gusts dangerously,

threatening to smash you into the ground you know must be waiting below, even

if it is out of sight.

"
