#82011
"A Break in the Narrow Trail"
"Obviously safer than the treacherous footing you can see to the south, the

trail has widened back to safely accomodate a wagon or even a brave caravan. 

A widened clearing lies to the east of the trail, the closeness of the

cliffside on the eastern side of the trail offering some limited shelter.  The

chasm edge is very close here, and you can see the sheer, icy wall of granite

tumbling away into a white eternity below.  The trail narrows again to the

north as it hugs the mountainside.

"
