#82012
"Mountainside Trail"
"Remarkably, the trail is nearly perfectly level, despite a sheer drop both on

the west into a widening chasm, and a nearly sheer cliff face climbing to the

east.  The clouds high above the mountain seem thinner here, making the craggy

granite of the cliff face on the eastern side of the trail all the more

intimidating.  Widening and sloping upward as it heads north, the trail

continues to hug the granite of the cliffside.

"
