countless times by travellers making their way through the pass.  The cleft to

the west winds around a corner, offering protection from the chill winds

outside.  The ceiling stretches high ahead, with a hole to vent smoke if one

were to build a fire.  The floor has been worn smooth over time, and a crude

firepit has been chiseled into the stone floor and surrounded with several

small rocks.

