#82014
"Hugging the Cliffside - Widening Trail"
"The trail continues to widen here, although unlike the level trail to the

south, the trail slopes sharply down towards the eastern side of the trail.  A

pile of ice and snow has collected along the eastern edge of the trail, next

to the mountainside.  All that seperates the edge of the trail on the west

from a deep drop into the chasm beyond is a thin ribbon of undisturbed snow --

apparently the animals in this area know what lies beyond.  The trail reaches

a peak and turns out of sight a bit to the north.

"
