#82015
"Mountainside Trail - Peak Along the Trail"
"This high point in the trail offers a spectacular view of the Dragonspires

which stretch away miles in the distance to the north and west.  A small

outcropping of ice-covered rock marks the furthest you can move north here

before a sheer drop into the yawning chasm; the trail turns to the east and

slopes down along the mountainside.  The trail is wide enough for a pair of

horses to comfortably ride abreast; wide indeed compared to the treacherous

footing below.  Footprints abound in the snow along the trail, humanoid, but

extremely large.

"
