hugging the cliffside.  While the cliff face to the south is sheer and covered

in ice, the eastern face is rough and clear of ice.  Beyond a crusted drift, a

chasm falls away; the stark peaks of the dragonspires visible in the distance

far beyond.  Recent activity is evident here -- the trail has been packed to

ice by the movement of large, humanoid creatures.

