#82017
"Before the Ice Bridge"
"Looming over the chasm sloping down into oblivion, a span seems to defy

gravity and crosses the chasm at its narrowest point to the north.  Running

parallel to the eastern cliff face, the trail is at its widest point since the

base of the mountains many miles below.  The trail here has been tracked down

to mushy ice by the travel of dozens of giant, humanoid creatures.  The

footprints in the snowy trail seem to stop abruptly a few feet before the icy

span -- perhaps the animals don't trust the bridge to hold them.


The remains of an ancient stone marker stand just west of the icy bridge.

"
