"Windscoured Chasm"
"The chasm is more narrow here than either north or south, forcing a biting

wind to whistle through from north to south.  The rock walls and even floor of

the chasm have been scoured smooth by hundreds or thousands of years of

snow-blowing wind, and are free from almost any frost, snow, or ice.  Faint,

blue-white trails can be made out along the rocky floor of the chasm.

