#82024
"Timeworn Stone Hall"
"Entombed in the ice, this ancient stone hall has survived unharmed for

uncountable eons.  The stone of the walls is carved from a speckled charcoal

stone; despite its obvious age, it shows no cracks from ice or other damage. 

There is no frost, dust, or debris collected here, even though your breath

fogs the air and metal rimes quickly with frost.  The western end of the hall

ends abruptly a few inches before a thick wall of ice begins -- perhaps where

the magic holding this chamber in such pristine condition ends and ordinary

stone once began.

"
"[Nereus] no.mob

"
