#82030
"Ransacked Stone Crypt"
"Once you imagine this room could have been a pristine crypt, a holy tribute to

the dead.  Now, it is difficult to imagine the glory of ages past.  The

northeastern corner of the room has completely collapsed, the charcoal-grey

stone lining the walls backed with dark speckled granite.  Writing must have

once lined all the walls in this chamber, but over ages past melting water

from the collapsing ceiling above has obliterated all but a few spidery runes

along the bases and near the tops of the walls.  The floor now slopes visibly

to the south; it appears water once ran from north to south through the room

and through a now dry crack in the southern edge of the floor.  A decaying

portal inset in the western wall leads out of this dead place.

"
""
