#82036
"Bottom of a Precipitous Chasm"
"Slick, ice-coated rock towers high above you to the north and south, except

for the base of the southern wall, which is a sheer sheet of opaque ice. 

Drifts of snow have piled against the bases of the icy walls of the chasm

here, while to the east and west, the chasm has collapsed far above, an

impassable avalanche of rock and ice.  It seems nothing can live here for

long; this icy chasm of rock and snow is inhospitable indeed.  High above,

barely visible on the northern wall of the chasm, you can make out a narrow

ledge.

"
