#82038
"North of a Narrow Bridge of Ice"
"A breathtaking bridge of opaque ice spans a chasm to the south.  Even though

it appears that further south, some of the bridge has collapsed over time, it

seems mostly stable.  Sloping up and away to the north, the trail disappears

in a virtual wall of snow; a blizzard of enormous proportions ebbs and flows,

but remaining relatively the same size.  The chasm horseshoes around the

bridgehead, apparently this is the only place the chasm is wide enough to span

easily.  There are scratches along the chasm wall just next to the bridge,

evidence of something climbing or being dragged over the snowy edge.

"
