#82040
"Through the Wall of Snow"
"A scene of terrible carnage, the snow has been churned about all around this

empty plateau.  Splatters of blood are evident in a dozen patches through the

snow, some bright red and some so dark almost to be black.  East and west of

this snowy plain, cliff edges abruptly drop into blackness; if it were snowing

here you have little doubt that it would be simple to wander off a cliff into

oblivion.  To the south, a blizzard rages, snow blown madly about from the

winds that blast across from east and west.

"
