#82041
"On a Precipitous Span of Ice"
"This bridge is a magnificent feat of engineering.  Made entirely of what

appears to be a single enormous block of ice, at one time this bridge likely

would have been wide enough to accomodate two wagons travelling side by side. 

Long ago, the western side of the bridge tumbled into the fissure below,

leaving only the eastern half wide enough to accomodate a brave horse and

rider.  A railing is visible on the east side, with evidence near the base

that it once had intricate carvings.  Whatever engineering or magic held this

bridge together appears to have weakened but the bridge as it is still seems

sturdy enough.

"
